Progresses give details on the advancement of a backup,.

USAGE:
  scw webhosting progress <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  get         Retrieve detailed information about a specific progress by its ID.
  list        List recent progresses associated with a specific backup, grouped by type.

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for progress
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw webhosting progress [command] --help" for more information about a command.
